@startuml seq-find
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because in-page find is a strict message sequence (open → type → debounce → fx →
'' paint → result back) spanning re-frame and a DOM-painting module, where activations, the generation
'' guard and the result-return arrow matter; PlantUML sequence gives autonumber + activation + concept
'' colour. Literal palette hexes: teal #2D9574 view, blue #4F97D7 re-frame, blue-violet #7590DB app-db,
'' green #67B11D the DOM/highlight.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title In-page find — shortcut ⟶ highlighted matches (CSS Custom Highlight API)

autonumber "<b>[0]"

actor User FS_TINT
participant "find-bar" as UI RENDERER_TINT
participant "keymap\nresolver" as KM RENDERER_TINT
participant "re-frame\nevents" as RF REFRAME_TINT
collections "app-db\n:ui/find" as DB APPDB_TINT
participant "re-frame\nfx" as FX REFRAME_TINT
participant "finder\n(renderer.find)" as F MARKDOWN_TINT
participant "find-scan\n(pure)" as S APPDB_TINT
participant "CSS.highlights\n+ DOM Ranges" as H MARKDOWN_TINT

== open the find bar ==
User -> KM : Ctrl+F  ·  vim "/"  ·  emacs C-s
KM -> RF : [:find/toggle]
activate RF
RF -> DB : :visible? true, **:gen++**
RF -> FX : fx :find/search {q gen}  //only if a query is remembered//
deactivate RF
DB --> UI : :ui/find sub → render <input auto-focus>

== type a query ==
User -> UI : type "the needle phrase"
UI -> RF : [:find/set-query q]
activate RF
RF -> DB : :query q, **:gen++**
RF -> RF : fx :async/debounce {key :find/search, 40 ms}\n**one live timer per key — re-arming REPLACES it**
deactivate RF
...debounce...
RF -> RF : [:find/run gen] — **drop unless gen = :ui/find/:gen**
RF -> FX : fx **:find/search {q gen}**
activate FX
FX -> FX : await **pdf-cache/ensure-active!**\n(materialize PDF text layers · drain a stream)
FX -> F : **finder/search! q**
activate F
F -> F : **cached buffer?** same doc, same root, no mutation since\n→ **reuse it** (the ordinary keystroke: 9 ms, not 304)\nelse **slice!** ::collect — TreeWalker over .vv-content,\nreject <script>/<style>/hidden/**<mjx-assistive-mml>**,\nclassify :inline / :soft / :hard (memoized by shape),\n**yielding every 8 ms**. NOT cancelled by a new query.
F -> S : **feed!** each token into the incremental builder\n(no token vector is ever materialized)
F -> S : **scan** buffer for the normalized query — **slice!** ::match,\ncancelled outright by the next keystroke
S --> F : <latex>[s, e)</latex> index pairs
F -> S : **locate** — invert <latex>\lambda</latex> at <latex>s</latex> and <latex>e-1</latex>
S --> F : (node, offset) pairs → **multi-node** Ranges
F -> H : Highlight.add(range) <latex>\forall</latex> matches, **in batches**\nCSS.highlights.set "vv-find" / "vv-find-current"
F -> H : **confined** scrollTo the Range's rect\n(:block :center — never el.scrollIntoView)
F --> FX : on-result {:count n :idx 1}\n//a superseded run never calls back//
deactivate F
FX -> RF : [:find/result {count idx **gen**}]
deactivate FX
activate RF
RF -> DB : bank BOTH scalars — **drop if gen is stale**
deactivate RF
DB --> UI : render "idx/n"

== cycle matches ==
User -> KM : F3 / Shift+F3  ·  vim n / N
KM -> RF : [:find/cycle ±1]
RF -> FX : fx :find/cycle {dir gen}
activate FX
FX -> F : **finder/cycle! dir**
activate F
F -> F : **reconcile** — doc-key changed → clear;\nmutation counter moved → **re-collect** (sliced), clamp cursor
F -> S : step-idx: <latex>\mathit{idx} := (\mathit{idx} + \mathit{dir}) \bmod n</latex>
F -> H : repaint "vv-find-current" + confined scroll
F --> FX : {:count n' :idx i}   //count too — a re-collect can change it//
deactivate F
FX -> RF : [:find/result …]
deactivate FX
RF -> DB : :count n', :idx i

== close ==
User -> UI : Escape  (or ×)
UI -> UI : blur → focus .vv-content **{preventScroll: true}**
UI -> RF : [:find/close]
RF -> DB : :visible? false, :gen++  //query is KEPT//
RF -> FX : fx :find/clear → finder/clear!\n(delete both highlights, disconnect the observer)

note over F, H #FFF6D6
  No DOM mutation: matches are painted as live Ranges via the CSS Custom
  Highlight API, styled by ::highlight(vv-find) / ::highlight(vv-find-current).
  A second payoff: CSS.highlights.set is not a mutation, so painting cannot
  re-trigger the MutationObserver that watches for a changed document.
  If unsupported, find degrades to no-op — the document is never altered.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Participant / concept |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| User |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| view (find-bar) + keymap resolver |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| re-frame events + effects |
  |<#7590DB>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| app-db :ui/find slice · pure find-scan |
  |<#67B11D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| finder + CSS.highlights painting (DOM) |
endlegend
@enduml
